Going live with a real provider had no way to fail well. The app spawns the
engine, the pane shows an error card, and the cause is several layers away:
a missing key, a key with no credit, a model id the account does not serve, or
CRUSORAI_BRIDGE_RUNNER still set — all of which look like "the agent is broken"
from inside the window.

The check resolves settings the same way the engine does, so what it prints is
what the app will see. Dry run by default (no network, no cost, no provider
SDK import); --live sends one 2-token request through `get_llm` — the engine's
own client, so a pass means the agent's path works, not merely that some HTTP
call succeeded. Failures go through the repo's own error classifier, which
names the fix (auth, billing, unknown model id). Keys are never printed: last
four characters and the length.

It also prints the fact that explains most "I set the key and it still fails":
src/config/settings.py loads .env with override=True, so the repo-root .env
beats an exported variable.

Four pins in src/tests/test_check_provider_script.py. Two matter: the
redaction never reveals a key (verified to fail when the redaction is
deliberately removed), and the provider list cannot drift from the factory —
parsed out of factory.py's `provider == "..."` dispatch, so adding a provider
there fails this test until the doctor knows it. A diagnostic that says "not
one of them" about a valid provider is worse than no diagnostic.

Also §7 of the desktop app-test runbook: where the key goes, why LLM_MODEL
matters as much as the key, running the check under .venv, relaunching (env
changes do not reach an already-spawned bridge), what each failure looks like
in the pane, and how to get back to free echo testing.

Verified here: dry run with a key present (exit 0), with nothing configured
(exit 1, names the missing variable), a typo'd LLM_PROVIDER, `custom` without
CUSTOM_BASE_URL, --live without the SDKs, and a leak check against a fake key
(absent from stdout and stderr). The live success path needs a real account and
is unverified by me. 119 passed, 1 skipped across the lanes that run here.

